{"kind": "mod", "id": 1398, "name": "Quieter Faceshield Breathing", "slug": "quieter-faceshield-breathing", "teaser": "Configurable volume for breathing with faceshield on!", "owner_name": "Arys", "downloads": 10759, "favourites": 0, "featured": false, "contains_ads": false, "contains_ai_content": false, "cheat_notice": false, "license_name": "MIT License", "guid": null, "thumbnail_local": null, "category": null, "category_id": null, "updated_at": "2026-07-13T18:05:25.000000Z", "created_at": "2024-05-12T04:38:32.000000Z", "published_at": "2024-05-12T04:38:32.000000Z", "latest_constraint": "~3.9.0", "latest_version": "1.0.1", "has_local": false, "has_github": false, "license_link": "https://choosealicense.com/licenses/mit/", "description_html": "<p>Very simple mod that was difficult to figure out how to implement thanks to how Unity and BSG handles audio sources.</p>\n<p>Use the BepInEx F12 config menu to change the volume (0-100%) of the faceshield breathing sound.</p>\n<p>Known issue: If you have faceshield on when loading into a raid, you will still hear the heavy breathing play out <strong>ONCE</strong> but will be silent from then onwards (I probably won’t fix this)</p>\n<p><strong>HOW TO INSTALL:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Download the mod</li>\n<li>Open the mod zip with 7-Zip (not WinRAR)</li>\n<li>Drag and drop the “BepInEx” folder straight into your SPT folder</li>\n</ol>\n", "versions": [{"version": "1.0.0", "spt_version_constraint": "~3.8.0", "content_length": null, "downloads": 3985, "published_at": "2024-05-12T04:38:32.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/1398/quieter-faceshield-breathing/1.0.0", "github_url": null, "external_url": null, "local_path": null, "fika_compatibility": "unknown", "dependencies": []}, {"version": "1.0.1", "spt_version_constraint": "~3.9.0", "content_length": null, "downloads": 6774, "published_at": "2024-07-08T22:05:56.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/1398/quieter-facesh